arktos (1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync pairing dialog: pairing code is a copyable read-only field
    with a Copy button (no more clipped/overlapping text); closing
    the dialog can no longer freeze the app on a blocked tor call;
    poll loop no longer piles queued calls onto a hung worker.

 -- Janos Szenfner <janos.szenfner@it-space.info>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100

arktos (1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Two engine flavors on every desktop package — servo + NoServo
    (QtWebEngine-only) variants, side-by-side installable.
  * Bundled tor updated to the 16.0 expert bundle.
  * Windows/macOS CI legs fixed (MSVC smoke-helper guards, NSIS
    license path, clang vexing-parse in tst_settingsdialog).

 -- Janos Szenfner <janos.szenfner@it-space.info>  Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0100

arktos (1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Full code audit (CA01-CA13): dead code removed, duplicate blocks
    consolidated, 8 security findings fixed (extension bridge
    subframe isolation, PDF path traversal, cert persistence),
    dying-object/lifetime fixes, adblock rebuild coalescing + DNR
    candidate index, Windows and macOS platform remediations.
  * Preferences sidebar adopts the Arktos-Mobile pastel-circle
    category icons.

 -- Janos Szenfner <janos.szenfner@it-space.info>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100

arktos (1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Hosted MV3 extension runtime: Bitwarden installs, unlocks and
    autofills (storage, ports, tabs messaging, nativeMessaging,
    permissions, offscreen, clipboard).
  * Serverless profile sync: per-profile device identity, embedded
    Tor onion transport, Noise_XX pairing, CRDT replication of
    bookmarks/history/tabs/settings, opt-in encrypted passwords,
    LAN fast path.
  * macOS: quit crash fix, extension popup rendering/sizing/anchor,
    urlbar completer, settings/proxy checkboxes, profile manager,
    Tor window tab button and start-page background.

 -- Janos Szenfner <janos.szenfner@it-space.info>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100

arktos (1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebrand to Arktos: the project formerly developed as Arora ships
    its first release as Arktos 1.0 (arktos-browser.com). Binary,
    install paths (/usr/lib/arktos, /usr/share/arktos), desktop file,
    icons and user data roots renamed; existing Arora config/data is
    migrated on first run.

